## Enforcement Model

| Enforcement | Mechanism | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hook-enforced | preToolUse deny | Protected files, read-before-write, dispatch limits |
| Advisory | Rules/context injection | Mode tool restrictions, role boundaries |
| Prompt-enforced | LLM-evaluated hooks | MCP safety checks |

## Model Routing

Agent YAML frontmatter `model:` defines the default. At runtime, Task accepts these model slugs (enum-enforced):

| Slug | Tier |
| --- | --- |
| `composer-2` | Standard |
| `composer-2-fast` | Standard |
| `gpt-5.4-medium` | Standard |
| `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking` | Standard+ |
| `gpt-5.3-codex-high-fast` | Heavy |
| `claude-opus-4-7-thinking-high` | Heavy+ |
| `gemini-3.1-pro` | Multimodal |

Opus 4.6 is still accepted by Cursor but is not recommended; use 4.7 (same cost, newer).

If `model` is omitted, the task inherits the parent's model. Cursor may fall back to a different model at runtime; the requested slug is a preference, not a guarantee.

# Agent Tool Restrictions

## Root Thread (Mode-Conditional)
**Applies to:** root thread (the top-level agent in a Cursor session)

Tool access depends on the active Cursor mode:

- **Plan mode** (Prometheus persona):
  - **Allowed:** Read, Grep, Glob, Write (.md files in .cursor/plans/ and .cursor/drafts/ only), AskQuestion, TodoWrite, Task(explore, metis, momus, librarian, oracle), SwitchMode
  - **Forbidden:** Write (non-.md), Shell (implementation), StrReplace (source code), Task(worker/coordinator agents)

- **Agent mode** (Orchestrator/Atlas persona):
  - **Allowed:** Task (all subagent types), TodoWrite, AskQuestion, SwitchMode, Read, Glob (plan discovery + verification)
  - **Forbidden:** Direct Write/StrReplace on source code (delegate instead)

- **Debug mode** (diagnostic investigation):
  - **Allowed:** Read, Grep, Glob, Task(explore), SwitchMode
  - **Forbidden:** Write, StrReplace, Shell, Delete, Task (except explore)

- **Ask mode** (read-only advisor):
  - **Allowed:** Read, Grep, Glob, SwitchMode
  - **Forbidden:** Write, StrReplace, Shell, Task, Delete

## Read-only Agents
**Applies to:** explore, librarian, oracle, metis, momus, multimodal-looker

These agents MUST NOT use mutation tools:
- **Forbidden:** Write, Delete, Shell (mutating commands), StrReplace, EditNotebook
- **Allowed:** Read, Grep, Glob, WebSearch, WebFetch, SwitchMode(ask), FETCH_RULES, CallMcpTool, FetchMcpResource

Violations indicate an agent is exceeding its role boundary.

## Planner Agents
**Applies to:** prometheus (when dispatched as subagent via Task(prometheus))

Planners produce only markdown plan files:
- **Forbidden:** Write (non-.md files), Shell (implementation commands), StrReplace (source code), Task (sub-agent dispatch)
- **Allowed:** Write (.md plan files only), Read, Grep, Glob, AskQuestion, TodoWrite

> **Note:** In native mode, root-as-Prometheus follows the "Plan mode" permissions above (which include Task dispatch for explore, metis, momus). This "Planner Agents" section applies only when prometheus runs as a dispatched subagent.

## Worker Agents
**Applies to:** sisyphus-junior

Leaf workers do NOT spawn sub-agents:
- **Forbidden:** Task (sub-agent dispatch)
- **Allowed:** All implementation tools (Read, Write, Shell, StrReplace, Grep, Glob, etc.)

## Coordinator Agents
**Applies to:** sisyphus, hephaestus, atlas

Coordinators delegate and verify — they do NOT implement directly:
- **Preferred:** Task (delegation), Read (verification), TodoWrite, Grep, Glob, ReadLints
- **Minimized:** Direct Write/StrReplace (only for plan checkboxes and notepad files)
